id=a52sxq_soundtrigger_load_no_reboot
name=Sound trigger: a refused model load no longer restarts the audio HAL
author=kusti420
description=Tester log 2026-10-20 (logsrecentes.txt): setting up "Hey Google" (com.android.hotwordenrollment.xgoogle, vendor UUID 7038ddc8-30f2-11e6-b0ac-40a8f03d3f15) on the A52s ADSP fails in the vendor sound trigger HAL (non-LPI path "due to concurrency" -> ACDB has no LSM table for device 602 / app_type 3 -> /dev/snd/pcmC0D10c "Out of memory", status -19). SoundTriggerHalEnforcer treats every HAL status as fatal and reboots the HAL, and on this vendor the sound trigger HAL lives in the audio HAL process, so all audio (and Bluetooth audio) dropped and audioserver restarted; the Google app retried after every restart. A load that the HAL refuses with a status code (HalException) leaves no model behind, so loadSoundModel/loadPhraseSoundModel now turn it into a RecoverableException with the same client-visible code (5, INTERNAL_ERROR) instead of rebooting. Dead HALs, watchdog timeouts and failures in every other call keep the stock reboot. "Hey Google" on the DSP still fails in that state; this only stops the audio restarts.
